@njhill First, I think focusing on disaggregated prefill/decode (P/D) would make the performance analysis more straightforward.

For PP decoding, without scheduler changes, workload imbalance across batches creates substantial pipeline bubbles, which inevitably hurts performance. I believe that making `pp_min_decode_batch_size` manually configurable allows us to tune the batching strategy to achieve strictly better performance than the current implementation.

Of course, this adds some framework complexity, but since the changes only affect PP-specific logic, I believe they are necessary to make PP effective for decode workloads.
